-- title:
--   Minimal primes over p label the components of the bad fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of `DRModelPackage p`, the structure that equips the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the modular curve of level $p$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$ with properness, flatness, integrality and normality data, models of its generic fibres over $\mathbb Q$ and over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with their Galois compatibilities, cusp sections, a smooth locus and the component morphisms `compInf`, `compZero`. Write $A$ for the $j$-finite chart ring `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ℤ F (jFull p)`, that is, the subalgebra of elements of $F=$`modularFunctionFieldFull p` integral over $\mathbb Z[j]$, and $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ for the chart morphism `ιFin` from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ to the model. Let $P\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,2\to$ ideals of $A$ be such that each $P i$ is prime, the minimal primes of the ideal generated by $p$ in $A$ are exactly $\{P 0, P 1\}$, and $P 0 \neq P 1$. The assertion is that there exists an index $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,2$, chosen uniformly in what follows, such that for every algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$ (in `Type`), every point $y$ of the base change of the model along $\mathbb Z \to k$, and every prime $\mathfrak q$ of $A$ with $\mathrm{pr}_1(y) = \iota_{\mathrm{fin}}(\mathfrak q)$ on underlying spaces: if $P j \not\subseteq \mathfrak q$ for every index $j \neq i$, then $y$ lies in the image of the underlying map of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ and not in the image of the underlying map of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the algebra of the $j$-finite chart ring at $p$ — its two minimal primes above $p$ — and the geometry of the characteristic-$p$ fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model, whose two irreducible components are distinguished by the cusp sections; the point of the statement is that one and the same index works for all algebraically closed fields $k$ of characteristic $p$. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_coordinate_forall_mem_range_compInf_and_not_mem_range_compZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_coordinate_forall_mem_range_compInf_and_not_mem_range_compZero), and its proof invokes the criterion [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_preimage_smoothLocus_iff_not_mem_range_compInf_inter_range_compZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_preimage_smoothLocus_iff_not_mem_range_compInf_inter_range_compZero) identifying the preimage of the smooth locus with the complement of the intersection of the two components.
